<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anton Günther, Count of Oldenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1583–1667</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Anton Günther of Oldenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anton Günther was Count of Oldenburg from 1603 until his death in 1667, and from 1647 also of Delmenhorst. Through careful diplomacy and payments to commanders he kept his county out of the fighting of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, and he won the lucrative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> toll at Elsfleth. Famous for breeding horses, he left no legitimate heir, and Oldenburg passed to the Danish crown.</p></div>
